{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nRepresentation drift (a schema/set/surface and a hand-maintained copy diverging) is the dominant sub-mechanism of the product-logic defect category (R2S1). Three mirror classes are already generated/gated (config↔docs via `gen_config_reference.py`, env-vars↔docs via `gen_env_registry.py`, library surface via `gen_api_surface.py`); the terminal-status set was unified by bug e63c; the MCP↔library gap is sibling story `cream-capitate-snake` (8ce5-b870-601d-4715). This task finds what else remains — unknown mirrors are unknown defect sources.\n\n## Approach\n\nSystematic sweep of `src/rebar` for hand-maintained duplicates of a canonical fact: enumerations duplicated across modules (status-like sets, error-code lists, event-type lists), doc tables restating code constants, schema fragments re-declared, hardcoded path/name lists mirroring a registry. Method: grep/AST passes for duplicate literal sets, cross-referenced with schemas and generators; each candidate is verified as a genuine mirror (same fact, two masters) rather than a distinct concept (the e63c audit's claimability-vs-terminal distinction). Deliverable is an inventory with dispositions; fixes land as follow-up tickets, not in this task.\n\n`reports/` is currently gitignored (`.gitignore` `/reports/`), so committing the deliverable requires re-including the `reports/stability/` subtree. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so the rule must become `/reports/*` plus a `!/reports/stability/` negation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` is committed, and lists every candidate examined with a verdict of `genuine mirror` / `distinct concept` / `already gated`. Verified by `git ls-files reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` printing the path.\n- [x] AC2: every finding carries `file:line` evidence for at least two masters. Verified by reading the report: each genuine-mirror row cites two or more locations.\n- [x] AC3: every genuine live mirror has a linked ticket created `discovered_from` this task, proposing generate-or-gate using an existing repo pattern. Verified by `rebar deps f9b9-83ad-931c-4833` listing those links.\n- [x] AC4: the inventory states the sweep method (the exact grep/AST patterns searched, and candidates examined per area) so the sweep is repeatable by a later reader.\n- [x] AC5: the sibling story's mirror (MCP↔library) is referenced as already-filed, not re-filed as a new ticket.\n- [x] AC6: `reports/stability/` is committable — the `.gitignore` rule is changed to `/reports/*` plus `!/reports/stability/`, and no other previously-ignored `reports/` content becomes tracked. Verified by `git status --porcelain reports/` showing only the intended file, and `git check-ignore -v reports/` still ignoring the parent.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis task ships a report plus a one-line `.gitignore` change; its verification is the committed-artifact and link checks named in the acceptance criteria, run from the worktree:\n\n- `git ls-files reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` — proves the deliverable is tracked (AC1) and that the `.gitignore` negation works (AC6).\n- `git status --porcelain reports/` — proves no unintended `reports/` content became tracked (AC6).\n- `rebar deps f9b9-83ad-931c-4833` — proves the `discovered_from` follow-up tickets exist and are linked (AC3).\n- `make lint` — proves the `.gitignore` edit breaks no existing gate (in particular the docs and deploy-manifest checks).\n\nNo new automated test is added: the change introduces no executable behavior, and the mechanism ratchet (sibling `unblacked-loveless-toad`) counts new gates rather than reports. A follow-up gate for any mirror found is scoped to that mirror's own ticket, not here.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` (new; committed inventory deliverable)\n- `.gitignore` (re-include `reports/stability/` so the deliverable can be committed)"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788336422089914001,"uuid":"3276d982-aa89-4e6e-92cd-203597040fee"}